<title>UK: GEC in Thomson talks with Lagardere, Alcatel.</title>
<headline>GEC in Thomson talks with Lagardere, Alcatel.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>British engineering and defence electronics company General Electric Co Plc said on Friday it was in talks with its partners Lagardre Groupe and Alcatel Alsthom over the privatisation of French electronics firm Thomson-CSF.</p>
<p>The French government said earlier that GEC was not eligible to bid for Thomson because the sale of more than 50 percent of Thomson was contrary to national security interests. Lagardere and Alcatel Alsthom have submitted bids.</p>
</text>
